     <p>
       The next generation, version 5, started when Bob Friesenhahn suggested improving the API so users could leverage algorithms from other languages or scripts. Bob wrote the C++ wrapper <code>Magick++</code> and contributed the module loader facility, automatic file identification, and test suites. Other notable contributors joined—Glenn Randers-Pehrson, William Radcliffe, and Leonard Rosenthol. As tens of thousands of users relied on it, a desire to freeze the API led to a fork by Bob and others, while I continued active development.
