   <p>Because ImageMagick ships in an open state for easy integration into containers and automated build pipelines, administrators must tighten policies to match production requirements. <strong class="text-warning-emphasis bg-warning-subtle px-1 rounded">The more untrusted input your application handles, the more restrictive your policy must be.</strong></p>
   <p>Policies are evaluated using a "last matching policy wins" model. For filesystem paths, ImageMagick evaluates canonical (fully resolved) paths and enforces canonical denies to block bypass attempts via symlinks, alternate representations, or path traversal tricks.</p>
