   <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mt-4 mb-3" id="environment"><i class="bi bi-sliders me-2 text-primary"></i>Selecting the Right Security Policy for Your Environment</h2>
   <p>To ensure optimal security in public-facing applications, you can restrict ImageMagick exclusively to web-safe formats like GIF, JPEG, and PNG. Alternatively, you can customize limits for memory allocation, allowed read/write paths, sequence frame counts, workflow runtime, and pixel cache disk space.</p>
   <p>Setting resource limits protects against malicious or malformed files—such as an internet-sourced image crafted to declare 20,000×20,000 dimensions. Without limits, such files can exhaust memory and disk space, causing system slowdowns or crashes. You can configure these limits in your <code>policy.xml</code> file.</p>
